{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"111644","commit":"981cb8736bbb2a622795ded00c6a5fe1c2267f20","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The change in `#CWST9` disables alternating sort by default. While this changes the behavior of the merge process (making it \"stable\" as indicated in the `toString` usage), it is a configuration change and does not introduce logical errors within the provided context.","nodes":[{"id":"libs/tdigest/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/MergingDigest.java-libs/tdigest/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/MergingDigest.java-3880:3884-3880:3885","promptId":"#CWST9","srcPath":"libs/tdigest/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/MergingDigest.java","dstPath":"libs/tdigest/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/MergingDigest.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":3880,"endPos":3884,"startLine":95,"startLineOffset":40,"endLine":95,"endLineOffset":44,"length":5}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":3880,"endPos":3885,"startLine":95,"startLineOffset":40,"endLine":95,"endLineOffset":45,"length":6}]}]},{"comment":"In `#HAP8A`, the addition of the check `if (lastUsedCell \u003d\u003d mean.length - 1)` is a necessary safety measure. Without it, if the internal buffers (`mean`, `weight`) were completely filled, the subsequent `else` block would increment `lastUsedCell` and attempt to access an index equal to the array length, resulting in an `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException`. Forcing `addThis \u003d true` when the buffer is full ensures that remaining values are merged into the final centroid rather than crashing the process.","nodes":[{"id":"libs/tdigest/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/MergingDigest.java-libs/tdigest/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/MergingDigest.java-11658:11695-11659:11706,11766:11908","promptId":"#HAP8A","srcPath":"libs/tdigest/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/MergingDigest.java","dstPath":"libs/tdigest/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/tdigest/MergingDigest.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":11658,"endPos":11695,"start